{"step_index":2543,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-27T12:27:51Z","thinking":"If a specific provider configuration lacks crucial connection details, the application likely attempts to complete this configuration through external data. A configuration object might be partially defined, but the application could consult a separate data source to retrieve the missing credentials and addresses. This approach would allow for flexible provider specification.\n\n\nThe provider configuration resolution process uses an external data file to augment incomplete configurations. This file lookup provides a fallback mechanism, ensuring that even minimal provider specifications from the user are enriched with complete connection details. Checking the import statements in the relevant server file confirms that the required modules for file system interaction and path manipulation are present.\n\n\nAdding necessary modules to the session-handling file and implementing the provider configuration resolver are the next steps. Examining the main web application's coordination logic is essential. Specifically, verifying how the main script manages and exposes various application components and views, including onboarding, hub, creation, and live interview states. The logic in the main script determines the display of these views based on the requested target view. The script updates the application's state manager based on user input.\n\n\nThe code initializes the live interview UI and checks for an existing connection. If no connection exists, a websocket connection is attempted. Audio processing is initiated, sending audio chunks via websocket. If audio processing fails, the session continues anyway, indicating a fallback mechanism. The `launchSession` function in the UI code prepares onboarding data. It attempts to start the interview using a global function, and if that function is not available, uses the websocket handler.\n\n\nThe application initiates the interview session by sending a message through the websocket handler with provider and onboarding data, and then manages UI views, hiding previous views and showing the live interview view. Subsequently, the session details are recorded in the history. The focus areas, such as coding and system design, are determined by calling the `getSelectedFocusAreas()` function in the UI script.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"\"Select-String -Path \\\"web/js/*.js\\\" -Pattern \\\"ai-providers-modal\\\" -Context 1,2\"","Cwd":"\"c:\\\\Users\\\\Arthur Henrique\\\\Documents\\\\GitHub\\\\Spectra\"","IsDaemon":"false","WaitMsBeforeAsync":"5000","toolAction":"\"Searching provider modal in web/js\"","toolSummary":"\"Search provider modal\""}}]}
